senses.gloss:
(I)--one of the four sons of शुक्र;
1: Br. III. 1. ७८, ८६; वा. ६५. ७७, ८५; Vi. I. १५. १२१.
married यशोधरा--वैरोचिनी, daughter of Virocana; father of त्रिशिर, विश्वरूप and विश्वकर्म;
2: Br. III. १४. 6; ५९. १७.
प्रह्रादी, another wife; सम्ज्ञा, a daughter of his, was given in marriage to the Sun God;
3: Ib. II. २४. ३४, ३९.
an आदित्य in the month of कार्त्तिक having ८००० rays;
4: Ib. II. २३. २०.
with the शिशिर Sun;
4: Ib. II. २३. २०.
reduced the Sun's तेजस्;
5: Ib. III. ५९. ४४ and ६५.
made विष्णु's discus;
6: Ib. III. ५९. ७१, ८२.
fell down on the earth for having drunk the Soma of शचिपति.
7: वा. ७८. 6; ९४. ५६.
